  "fallback": {
    "text": "A weighted graph has A-B 4, A-C 1, C-B 2 and B-D 1, all nonnegative. Dijkstra starts at A with B at 4 and C at 1 in the frontier. C is finalized at 1; relaxing C-B lowers B to 3. B is finalized at 3; relaxing B-D lowers D from 6 to 4. D is finalized at 4, giving the shortest path A-C-B-D with cost 1+2+1=4. The first route found, A-B-D at 5, is not shortest. A node is finalized only at its smallest tentative distance, and relaxation updates a distance only when the new route is smaller. Negative weights would invalidate that greedy finalization."
  },
